  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Most people carry an English first name and a name in their own language, and either can be the one friends use. Shona names are full sentences with a meaning, often thanks or hope addressed to God: Tatenda (we are thankful), Tinashe (God is with us), Kudakwashe (God's will), Rutendo (faith). Many are unisex. English names are often virtues or wishes: Blessing, Patience, Precious, Lovemore, Learnmore, Givemore. The family name comes from the father; every family also has a totem (mutupo in Shona, isibongo in Ndebele) such as Moyo (heart), Shumba (lion), Ncube or Dube (zebra), used as a polite way to address someone. Ndebele names follow the Nguni pattern (Sibusiso, Nomsa) and many Harare families of Malawian or Zambian heritage carry Chewa surnames like Banda, Phiri and Tembo.",
